~ start

# ECHO//LINE — Echo Greeting (Past Timeline)
# Used when a player first enters the Past timeline.
# Title and balloon are configured in Dialogue Manager settings.

if Engine.has_singleton("DialogueManager") or ClassDB.class_exists("DialogueManager"):
	# Dialogue Manager is enabled: this file is loaded directly via
	# DialogueManager.show_dialogue_balloon_scene().
	pass

do intro_echo
intro_echo: The wind carries whispers of an ancient era. Stones still hum with forgotten hymns.
do intro_echo_2
intro_echo_2: As the Past player, your foundation shapes all that follows.
do intro_echo_3
intro_echo_3: What will you build first?

=> Build the foundation of the clock tower > END
=> Tend the gardens of the courtyard > END
=> Inscribe the archive tablet > END

~ end
do memory_saved
memory_saved: Your choices echo forward. The Present stirs.
=> Continue > END

~ start

# ECHO//LINE — Clockmaker First Meeting
# Triggered when player approaches the Clockmaker NPC in the Present timeline.

do clockmaker_greeting
clockmaker_greeting: Welcome, traveler. The mechanism falters. I am the Clockmaker — keeper of temporal balance.
do clockmaker_choice
clockmaker_choice: Will you aid me, or watch time unravel?

=> I will help. Tell me what to do. > END
=> What happens if I refuse? > END
=> Who are you, really? > END

~ end
do clockmaker_grateful
clockmaker_grateful: I knew you would choose wisely. Begin at the courtyard — the Past holds the key.
=> Continue > END

~ start

# ECHO//LINE — Tutorial Step 1
# Triggered at the start of the Tutorial scenario.

do tutorial_intro
tutorial_intro: Welcome to ECHO//LINE. You inhabit one of three fractured timelines.
do tutorial_intro_2
tutorial_intro_2: Across each, your actions ripple.
do tutorial_intro_3
tutorial_intro_3: Together, you must stabilize reality before catastrophe.

=> Continue > tutorial_step_2

~ tutorial_step_2
do tutorial_step_2_line
tutorial_step_2_line: Tap any glowing object in your timeline to interact.
do tutorial_step_2_line_2
tutorial_step_2_line_2: Watch for ripple effects in other timelines — your choices echo forward and backward.

=> Got it > END

~ end
do tutorial_complete
tutorial_complete: You are ready. Find your timeline. Choose your role. Begin.
=> Begin > END
